+# FPT 2026 Venue Requirements
+
+Checked: `2026-08-02`
+
+Primary source: [FPT 2026 Call for Papers](https://fpt2026.uark.edu/call-for-papers/)
+
+## Conference-Track Rules
+
+| Requirement | Official rule | Current artifact status |
+|---|---|---|
+| Format | PDF in IEEE style | PASS at source level: `paper/corrected/paper.tex` uses `IEEEtran` conference mode. |
+| Page size | US Letter | PASS at source level: no A4 option is set. Final PDF media boxes remain `NOT_RUN`. |
+| Full-paper length | Up to 8 content pages, with unlimited reference pages | `NOT_RUN` until an authorized audit PDF exists. |
+| Review anonymity | Author names and affiliations must be absent for double-blind review | PASS at source level: the manuscript uses `Anonymous Authors` and has no acknowledgement section. Final PDF metadata inspection remains `NOT_RUN`. |
+| Submission route | Conference-track papers use the FPT 2026 HotCRP site | External submission action; no upload is authorized. |
+| Artifact form | Due July 31, 2026, Anywhere on Earth | The listed deadline has elapsed. The author must confirm whether an artifact form was already filed. |
+
+## Calendar State
+
+The official page lists the conference-track title/abstract and full-paper
+deadlines as June 19, 2026; rebuttal as July 24--31, 2026; artifact form as
+July 31, 2026; and notification as August 21, 2026. As of this check, the
+submission, rebuttal, and artifact-form dates have elapsed. This repository
+does not infer submission state from those dates and performs no external
+submission action.
+
+## Final Checks
+
+When the evidence gates authorize an audit candidate:
+
+1. Verify that content ends by page 8 and that any later pages contain references only.
+2. Verify every PDF page uses a US Letter media box.
+3. Inspect visible text and PDF metadata for author, affiliation, acknowledgement, grant, repository-owner, and path disclosures.
+4. Confirm all fonts are embedded and all figures, tables, captions, references, and margins are legible.
+5. Recheck the official venue page before human submission review because conference instructions can change.
