+\end{tabular}
+\end{table}
+
+\section{Numerical Method}
+\subsection{Uniform MXFP4 Path}
+The matched BF16 comparator rounds state and operands to BF16 at their declared
+boundaries and performs reductions in FP32. The MXFP8-state fallback changes
+only the recurrent state to eight-bit E4M3 elements under E8M0 B32 scales while
+retaining MXFP4 token operands; flat INT4 uses signed symmetric four-bit quantization
+with a tensor-wide scale.
+
+We report a floating Q/DQ MXFP4 diagnostic and a distinct native encoded path.
+The Q/DQ diagnostic quantizes at named boundaries but performs the intervening
+recurrence in floating point. It does not represent the HLS accumulator or its
+event behavior. The encoded path below is the software counterpart of the
+native HLS arithmetic.
+
+The uniform path stores E2M1 elements in B32 blocks with an E8M0 scale per
+block. For nonzero block maximum $m$ and largest finite E2M1 magnitude
+$x_{\max}$, the selected scale power is
+$s=\lceil\log_2(m/x_{\max})\rceil$; its biased E8M0 code is clamped to the
+valid range. Elements are divided by $2^s$ and rounded to E2M1 with RNE. Zero
+has a canonical encoding. If E2M1 magnitude code $r$ denotes $r/2$, a product
+has integer magnitude $r_a r_b$ and power $s_a+s_b-2$.
+One flat 128-term reduction aligns every product directly to the greatest nonzero product exponent (power),
+applies RNE to the full exponent-difference shift, and accumulates in ascending
+key-index order with signed \CorrectedAccumulatorBits{}-bit saturation after
+every addition. A nonzero term rounded to zero is counted as an alignment
+underflow. This uniform baseline has no guard-bit offset; the five guard bits
+described below belong only to the corrected candidate.
+
+Each synthetic STEP record supplies normalized $q$ and $k$, value $v$, decay
+$\alpha$, delta gate $\beta$, and the selected initial state $S$. The MXFP4
+paths encode $q$, $k$, $v$, and every state write; $\alpha$ and $\beta$ use
+unsigned Q1.15 fixed point. There are no projection weights in a test vector
+because all projections are outside the recurrence-core boundary. The MXFP8
+fallback changes only state element codes to E4M3 under B32 E8M0 scales; flat
+INT4 changes the same token operands and state under its declared tensor-wide
+scale. Requantization, element and accumulator saturation, scale clamps,
+alignment underflows, and scale changes are explicit state-write events. The
+complete contract is versioned in the artifact rather than inferred from C++
+types.
+
+The element product uses sign exclusive-or (XOR), table-based E2M1 magnitude
+multiplication, and exponent addition. No floating-point type appears in the
+active native arithmetic sources. The resulting E2M1 element-product logic is
+integer based;
+wider coefficient operations may still map to DSPs and are reported as such.
+
+\subsection{Recurrence-Aware Correction}
+Native encoded MXFP4 fails the frozen finite-trace thresholds, so we also
+evaluate one locally frozen correction. The base state has an E2M1 primary term and a dense
+signed \CorrectedEZeroResidualBits{}-bit E2M0-style residual, each with B32
+scales. \CorrectedResidualStackTerms{}-term residual-stacked E2M1 vectors
+represent token inputs and live rank-one writes.
+Up to \CorrectedLogCapacity{} writes remain in a log with Q1.15 decay
+coefficients. At capacity, all \CorrectedLogCapacity{} entries are folded
+tilewise into the base and the log is cleared.
+This candidate aligns shared exponents with \CorrectedAlignmentGuardBits{}
+guard bits before signed \CorrectedAccumulatorBits{}-bit accumulation.
+
+This representation is a mitigation, not the controlled uniform replacement.
+It changes the physical state representation and adds a periodic fold. Its
+logical payload is \CorrectedLogicalStateBytes{} bytes per layer, only
+\CorrectedBytesBelowMxfpEight{} bytes below a uniform
+MXFP8-E4M3-B32 state. Exact arithmetic equivalence was tested separately before
+quantized evaluation.
+
+\section{FPGA Implementation}
+Both controlled baselines use equivalent persistent-state command semantics and
+the same five-phase token organization. Commands select one of
+\CorrectedNumLayers{} runtime layer slots and support RESET, LOAD, STEP, and
+READBACK. Their data-plane encodings are not identical: BF16 transports BF16
+tensors, whereas MXFP4 transports encoded elements and scales and returns
+expanded integer output fields. Packing and token quantization are outside both
+HLS kernels. Before interface packing, a STEP consumes
+\CorrectedBfSixteenStepInputBytes{} logical input bytes in the BF16 kernel and
+\CorrectedUniformMxfpFourStepInputBytes{} in the uniform MXFP4 kernel; the
+corrected residual-stack candidate consumes
+\CorrectedCandidateStepInputBytes{}. BF16 returns
+\CorrectedBfSixteenOutputBytes{} logical output bytes, while the native kernels'
+expanded INT32-mantissa/INT16-exponent fields total
+\CorrectedNativeExpandedOutputBytes{}. These are type-layout counts, not
+measured AXI traffic; RESET has no tensor payload, and resident-state LOAD and
+READBACK use their separately reported logical state payloads. The HLS target is
+\texttt{xcu55c-fsvh2892-2L-e} under Vitis HLS
+\CorrectedHlsToolVersion{} at \CorrectedTargetClockNs{} ns with
+$P_K=\CorrectedPk$, $P_V=\CorrectedPv$, and B32.
+We retain the U55C target used by the inherited BF16 dataflow so the arithmetic
+comparison does not also change devices. We fix this target and parallelism
+point for the replacement rather than tune each format independently.
+
+The corrected candidate adds packed primary and residual banks,
+\CorrectedLogCapacity{} packed key/update log entries, per-head gamma and lambda
+coefficients, and event counters. A non-mutating snapshot exposes all
+persistent fields for exact verification. Folding is atomic at the command
+boundary.
+
+Figure~\ref{fig:datapath} maps the correction onto the inherited five-phase
+schedule. The base state remains resident while each STEP decays its
+coefficient, evaluates the base and live writes, appends the new rank-one
+update, and reads the output from the updated logical state. When the
+\CorrectedLogCapacity{}-entry log fills, a tilewise fold runs after the output
+has observed the newest write.
+
